**Finding:** plot_constraint_summary on the 900-1300 GeV x 300-650 keV scan returns best fit m_chi=986 GeV, delta=350 keV (plot /Users/nramachandra/github-integration/inelastic-dm-server/output/constraint_summary.png); this lies below both the 475 keV (IceCube, 2609.01590) and 557 keV (Super-K+IceCube, 2609.07807) solar-neutrino exclusion lines, so under the tool's truncated SHM (v_max=776 km/s) no point reproducing the LZ event survives the neutrino limits, and the 2609.01590 region (481-519 keV) requires a high-velocity tail (e.g. LMC) not modelled by the tool.
