[finding] f-026 Gamma-ray line status at about 1.1 TeV (2609.01590): at the joint best-fit mass the thermal higgsino line prediction is 0.815-0.900 of the H.E.S.S. observed lim
**Finding:** Gamma-ray line status at about 1.1 TeV (2609.01590): at the joint best-fit mass the thermal higgsino line prediction is 0.815-0.900 of the H.E.S.S. observed limits (546 h), so it is close to but not excluded. The matched CTAO Alpha 500 h projection gives mu_gamma,95 = 1.69, which is above the thermal target. The estimate for the Omega configuration, 1.69/2 = 0.85, is below mu_gamma = 1, so the thermal target is within CTAO exclusion reach. Dwarf, CMB and ATLAS disappearing-track limits do not exclude the region.
