**Finding:** Abstract-level only: 2610.03692 (Freese and Theodosopoulos) finds the 1.1 TeV thermal higgsino only marginally compatible with the LZ event and IceCube, and only with the LMC tail, no elastic solar cooling and no LZ high-energy sideband. Its compatible regions extend from about 2 TeV to hundreds of TeV, with delta about 350-525 keV. 2609.09830 computes one-loop EW corrections, with on-shell renormalization reducing delta_m and Higgs-exchange elastic and inelastic rates; the abstract gives no number for the size of the change. 2609.06890 proposes light boosted DM whose energy is set by the dark-sector spectrum, so it is independent of the halo tail.
