**Critic, wave 1** — continue: 5 findings stand up to the evidence, 5 questioned ('check_all_constraints at m_chi = 1160 GeV returns 'VIABLE' for delta = 400, 500 and 600 ke': The quoted excerpts of tc-...-38/39/40 stop at the 'cmb_energy_injection' key. Neither the CMB p_ann values (0.86, 1.35, 1.94 e-45 against 3.2e-28) nor the overall 'VIABLE' verdict appears in the evidence. The relic, LZ and Fermi numbers do match. Re-quote the full JSON before treating the CMB and verdict parts as supported.; '2609.01590 (Wu, Zhang, Zhu) finds LZ-preferred delta_m = 481-519 keV (1 sigma) and 475-529': Neither evidence excerpt contains the claimed numbers. tc-...-32 is the title and author page, and tc-...-36 is the Fig. 3 gamma-ray caption. Neither shows 481-519, 475-529, 312-422, 280-457, 366 keV, 1.09 TeV, 1000-1183 GeV or 943-1230 GeV. The d-12 summary also says the cite tool rejected these sentences (x-04). The values may be correct, but they are not evidenced.; 'The 475 keV and 557 keV neutrino lines differ because of how the captured population in th': Only part of the claim is evidenced. tc-...-37 supports the LMC/substructure rescue statement, and tc-...-45 shows the chi^2 procedure. No excerpt contains 475, 466, 454, 553 or 557 keV, the halo parameters (220/544/232 km/s), <sigma v> = 1.3e-26 or 1.5e-26, or m_chi = 1.08/1.11 TeV. There is also a labelling issue: tc-...-45 sets the limit at Delta chi^2 = 2.71, which is the one-sided 95% (two-sided 90%) threshold. This should be stated explicitly when comparing with the 90% CL IceCube line of 2609.01590.; 'Gamma-ray line status at about 1.1 TeV (2609.01590): at the joint best-fit mass the therma': tc-...-36 shows only that Fig. 3 plots H.E.S.S. and CTAO Omega curves of mu_gamma over 950-1200 GeV. The 0.815-0.900 ratio, the 546 h exposure and mu_gamma,95 = 1.69 do not appear in any excerpt. It is also unclear whether '1.69/2 = 0.85' comes from the paper or is the agent's own estimate. tc-...-44 concerns solar thermalization and is not relevant to the gamma-ray claim.).

Issues: The central task question has not been answered quantitatively: where does the elastic SI cross section of the thermal higgsino sit relative to the LZ 4.2 t-yr and XENONnT 90% CL curves at 1.0-1.2 TeV? No finding gives either the higgsino SI value (loop and Higgs-mediated, around 1e-48 to 1e-49 cm^2 with possible cancellation) or the limit values at 1.1 TeV. d-11 is still open, and this comparison is the core of the headline answer.; The thermal mass of about 1159 GeV is set by the tool's hard-coded normalization (sigma_v = 2.5e-26 x (1100/m)^2). It is a calibration, not a computation. The report must not present it as an independent check of 1411.6930. The Sommerfeld/coannihilation step and the charged-splitting sensitivity in the brief were never done. A literature or analytic estimate (1008.2905 method) is needed if the task's 'with and without Sommerfeld' item is to be answered.; The tool's indirect-detection and CMB passes rest on a p-wave, splitting-suppressed annihilation today. This is unphysical for a higgsino, which annihilates s-wave to WW/ZZ at about 1-1.5e-26 cm^3/s. The 'VIABLE' label for indirect and CMB constraints should be replaced by a comparison of the s-wave rate with the Fermi dwarf and H.E.S.S. continuum and line limits at 1.1 TeV, together with f-026..
