[finding] f-030 2609.09830 (Chatterjee et al.) gives no on-shell delta_m shift in the 300-600 keV range. Its benchmarks are tuned so the one-loop on-shell (CCN[n] scheme) neutr
**Finding:** 2609.09830 (Chatterjee et al.) gives no on-shell delta_m shift in the 300-600 keV range. Its benchmarks are tuned so the one-loop on-shell (CCN[n] scheme) neutral splitting is delta = 36.37, 8.90, 16.39, 10.81 and 10.59 keV for BP1-BP5 (|mu| = 0.61-1.40 TeV; all have Omega h^2 < 0.12, so the relic constraint is not imposed). The tree-to-one-loop shift can be read from the Table III masses: about 0.14 GeV tree splitting vs 0 at one loop for BP1 (739.55/-739.69 to 739.33/-739.33 GeV), i.e. O(10-100) MeV scale. This paper therefore does not bear on the 475-557 keV window.
