**Blocked — Recover quoted evidence for the contested literature numbers (f-024, f-025, f-026, f-027), and replace the tool's unphysical p-wave indirect-detection pass with an s-wave higgsino comparison at 1.1 TeV..** (The tool budget ran out before the 2609.01590 and 2609.07807 text windows could be read and before the indirect-detection comparison could be done.) Two of the four goals are settled from full texts. The other two, plus the indirect-detection comparison, were not reached. (1) 2609.09830 does not give an on-shell delta_m shift for the 475-557 keV window (f-030). Its benchmark points are tuned to small one-loop on-shell splittings: delta = 36.37, 8.90, 16.39, 10.81 and 10.59 keV for BP1-BP5, at |mu| = 0.61-1.40 TeV, all with Omega h^2 < 0.12. Comparing its tree and one-loop masses suggests the shift is of order 0.1 GeV, but that is my reading of their mass table, not a number the paper states. So the paper is not relevant to rescuing the 475-557 keV window. (2) 2610.03692 defines four IceCube treatments, shown at 90% CL in its Fig. 2 (f-031): capture-annihilation equilibrium; SI inelastic cooling only; SI inelastic + SD elastic cooling; and SI inelastic + SD + SI elastic cooling with sigma_SI,el = 4e-50 cm^2. Its inputs: W+W- limits, standard halo with v0 = 220, v_sun = 232 and v_esc = 544 km/s, rho = 0.3 GeV/cm^3, and an LMC tail cut off at v_min = 950 km/s. The solar limits are stated not to change when the LMC is added. The delta values at 1.1 TeV for each treatment appear only in the figure, so they are not quantified. The paper's text calls the 1.1 TeV thermal higgsino only marginally compatible. Blocked items (dead end x-06): the tool budget ran out before narrow re-reads of 2609.01590 and 2609.07807. Findings f-024, f-025 and f-026 therefore remain contested, including whether the 1.69/2 CTAO Omega estimate is from the paper or from the agent. No s-wave <sigma v> versus H.E.S.S. ratio was computed, so the tool's p-wave pass (f-022) is still unreplaced. The full texts are in /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-higgsino-dd/runs/261022_110244/ as 2609.01590.txt, 2610.03692.txt and 2609.09830.txt. No cite calls were made.
