**Finding:** Under the tool's truncated SHM (v_max = 776 km/s), the LZ-compatible band (0.3-5 events, 2.84 t-yr) for m_chi = 1000-1200 GeV is confined to delta of about 350 keV. predict_recoil gives N = 10.67/17.30 at delta = 340 keV (m_chi = 1000/1183 GeV), 1.13/2.90 at 350 keV (1000/1200 GeV), 0.03/0.158 at 360 keV (1000/1183 GeV) and 0.00/0.00 at 380 keV. A 16x16 scan (m_chi 1000-1200 GeV, delta 330-480 keV in 10 keV steps) reports exactly 16 points in the 0.3-5 band, best fit (1000 GeV, 350 keV). No LZ-compatible point has delta >= 475 keV, or even >= 360 keV.
