**Finding:** Analytic kinematics (m_N = 122.0 GeV for Xe-131, E_R = 248 keV, sqrt(2 m_N E_R) = 0.8206 keV per km/s): delta_max = v_max*sqrt(2 m_N E_R) - m_N E_R/mu gives, at m_chi = 1000/1100/1183 GeV, 358.5/361.3/363.2 keV for v_max = 776 km/s, 378/381/383 keV for 800 km/s, 419/422/424 keV for 850 km/s and 460/463/465 keV for 900 km/s. This reproduces the tool's v_min(248 keV) to within 1 km/s (766 vs 765.7 km/s at 1000 GeV and 350 keV; 921/969/1018 km/s at 1100 GeV and 480/520/560 keV). The tool's 'about 365 keV' edge is the E_R-optimized endpoint delta_max = mu v_max^2/2 = 364/368/370 keV at 776 km/s, reached at E_R = mu*delta/m_N of about 330 keV, not at 248 keV.
